{"kind":"propose","text":"E3 compatibility found that a normal C4 publication with pending custody has no synchronous checked source-version proof. The retained signing holds an authorization identity and position, but resolving it requires a new storage await. A focused timing case already failed when that await also ran for an empty C4 publication. The empty shortcut passed the focused owners, but it leaves the new await for nonempty existing C4 callers. I propose an explicit unavailable row arm for a modern pending row whose source has not been checked, whether the caller has not opted in or retained authorization is unavailable. It keeps C4 display, lookup and publication timing, supplies no ref field, and makes E3 action exploration unavailable. The separate legacy arm keeps ref: null and the legacy custody reason. The opted-in verified arm publishes the exact checked ref and preserves pending-to-recorded association. This keeps old callers and their I/O paths unchanged. Please decide that row arm before the public type is finalized."}